{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Sickness feels like a natural next choice because my recent interest in Ten Thousand Fists makes me want more of Disturbed's aggressive riffs and vocals.",
    "Shot to Hell, Reign In Blood and Vulgar Display of Power connect with different parts of my heavier listening: melodic vocals over heavy riffs, fast aggression and forceful grooves."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adore's subdued atmosphere and The Best of Chicago's polished pop rock miss the heavy guitars and intensity I want right now.",
    "I passed on Monster and Above because I could not confidently identify those albums from their titles; that uncertainty does not mean I dislike their music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some rock albums seems to have been stretched into an interest in rock broadly, even when the sound lacks the weight I am seeking.",
    "Chuck makes punk energy relevant to me, but that connection alone does not make International Superhits! a priority over heavier choices today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening to Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days gives stronger context for today's choices than my earlier interest in lighter music.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I choose now: United Abominations appeals to my interest in thrash, but the Disturbed connection and heavy grooves draw me more immediately."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but some choices stretched broader rock connections beyond the intensity and specific sounds I want today."
}"}
